  "description": "Swiss chard is cooked with plenty of garlic, olive oil, serrano, and lemon for a tender, punchy green side dish that pairs with almost any meal.",
  "notes": "Notes: Swiss chard stems have a pleasant crunch and mild, earthy flavor. To include them, thinly slice the stems and add them once the garlic has softened but before it begins to brown. Cook until crisp-tender, then add the serrano and proceed with the recipe.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.",
